WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.920
Cluely AI has stirred up a lot of controversy&nbsp;
for supposedly helping people cheat in exams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.040
coding interviews, and even sales calls.
But is it really this game-changing assistant…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:17.360
or just another overhyped meeting notetaker?
In this video, we’re going to test Cluely AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.840
in detail to see how it actually&nbsp;
performs when it matters most.&nbsp;

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.960
You will find the links to all the exclusive&nbsp;
discounts in the description below.&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.080
Start by downloading its desktop app&nbsp;
on Mac or Windows and logging in.&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.480
As soon as you do that, you’ll notice a&nbsp;
small Cluely widget appear at the top of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:42.000
your screen - that’s your main control center.
When you register for the first time, Cluely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.920
automatically launches a short built-in tutorial&nbsp;
that walks you through what every button does.&nbsp;

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.240
It’s clean, minimal, and honestly&nbsp;
quite intuitive - even if you’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:58.400
never used a productivity assistant before.
Now let’s start using Cluely in a real scenario.&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.640
Once your app is ready, click the&nbsp;
“Start Cluely” button - that’s how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.080
you tell Cluely to start recording and analyzing&nbsp;
everything that’s being said in your meeting.&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.080
It’s important to note that Cluely&nbsp;
doesn’t record video - it only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:18.160
listens to audio and screen activity, so your&nbsp;
conversations stay focused and lightweight.&nbsp;

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.160
During your meeting, you can&nbsp;
actually talk to Cluely in real time.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:27.760
For example, if you zone out or miss&nbsp;
something important, just press Ctrl + Enter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:32.240
Cluely will automatically assist you and&nbsp;
provide you with the recent information.&nbsp;

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.280
Or you can type:&nbsp;

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.960
“What did I miss just now?”
 
Cluely instantly processes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:42.880
the conversation and gives you a clear,&nbsp;
concise response - right inside the widget.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:49.440
Since Cluely is a standalone desktop app, it&nbsp;
runs smoothly across all major platforms - Zoom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.760
Google Meet, Microsoft Teams,&nbsp;
or even phone call recordings.&nbsp;

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.560
Let’s go through its main features one by one.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.640
First, there’s Show Transcript.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.160
Just click “Transcript,” and&nbsp;
Cluely instantly displays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:05.760
everything that’s being said - live, in real time.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.800
It’s clean, well-formatted, and makes it&nbsp;
super easy to scroll back and catch key&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.720
moments you might’ve missed.
Next is Generate Summary.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:21.920
At any point, you can ask Cluely to summarize your&nbsp;
entire conversation or just the last few minutes.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.000
It delivers a quick, structured&nbsp;
overview - perfect for meetings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.880
that run too long or when you need&nbsp;
instant notes right after a call.&nbsp;

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.640
Then comes Ask Questions.
For example you can ask it for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:39.040
a quick recap or even for follow-up&nbsp;
questions regarding the meeting.&nbsp;

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.680
You can literally type any context-based&nbsp;
question about what’s happening on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.880
your screen or what’s being discussed.
And here’s something advanced users will love:&nbsp;

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:54.000
You can also create a knowledge base by&nbsp;
uploading your company or product information.&nbsp;

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:00.480
That way, during calls, Cluely can reference your&nbsp;
own materials - making it incredibly useful for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:06.960
sales teams, customer support, or even training&nbsp;
sessions where accurate information matters.&nbsp;

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.280
Now let’s talk about something Cluely&nbsp;
is known for - Invisibility Mode.&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:16.880
To access it, click at your account at the top&nbsp;
of your Cluely dashboard and select settings.&nbsp;

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:22.320
This takes you straight into the Settings panel.
Here, you’ll find an option labeled “Detectable”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.280
or “Undetectable.”
Simply toggle between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.920
the two depending on your needs.
You can also toggle it using control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:35.200
plus slash on Windows and command&nbsp;
plus slash on Mac as a shortcut.&nbsp;

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:40.480
When “Undetectable” mode is turned on,&nbsp;
Cluely runs completely in the background.&nbsp;

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.840
Meeting participants won’t see&nbsp;
that it’s active, and it won’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:49.600
appear in your recordings or shared screens.
But this feature isn’t reliable, doesn’t work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:55.680
for all platforms and it’s better you don’t use&nbsp;
it in important meetings like coding interviews.&nbsp;

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:59.360
Once your meeting wraps up, it’s&nbsp;
time to review your results.&nbsp;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:03.520
Start by clicking the “Record” button&nbsp;
again - that stops the active session.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:08.720
Then head over to the Home icon on the sidebar,&nbsp;
where you’ll find a list of all your recent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:12.160
meetings neatly organized.
Open any session,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:18.320
and you’ll see everything Cluely captured:
The full transcript,Your AI-generated notes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:23.600
And any questions you asked during the meeting.
From here, you can take things further.&nbsp;

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:29.920
Ask Cluely to write a follow-up email, re-generate&nbsp;
a summary, or even copy the transcript manually if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:34.080
you’d like to store it elsewhere.
Coming to privacy and security:&nbsp;

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:40.160
Cluely claims it doesn’t sell and train on your&nbsp;
data. But independent tests have exposed that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:46.880
suffers from serious security vulnerabilities.
Now, let’s quickly go over Cluely AI’s pricing:&nbsp;

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:50.480
Starting with the Free Plan -&nbsp;
this one gives you limited access,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:54.480
allowing up to five Pro responses&nbsp;
per day which is good enough if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.880
you just want to test Cluely or use&nbsp;
it occasionally for short meetings.&nbsp;

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.560
Next is the Pro Plan, priced&nbsp;
at 20 dollars per month.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:08.480
This version removes all restrictions, giving you&nbsp;
unlimited responses both during and after meetings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:14.480
- perfect if you rely on Cluely for regular&nbsp;
work calls, interviews, or client sessions.&nbsp;

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:21.520
Now, before you rush to install Cluely, let’s talk&nbsp;
about a few important drawbacks you should know.&nbsp;

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.960
First, Cluely doesn’t currently support direct&nbsp;
integrations with tools like Slack, Notion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:32.160
or CRM platforms, so if you want to organize&nbsp;
your meeting notes elsewhere, you’ll need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:38.880
to export them manually or use merge dot dev.
Then there are the ethical and legal concerns.&nbsp;

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:45.440
Because Cluely can operate in a hidden or overlay&nbsp;
mode, it raises valid issues around consent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:49.680
misrepresentation, and fairness -&nbsp;
especially if someone uses it in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:55.360
exams or interviews without disclosing it.
Performance-wise, response times can lag&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.360 --> 00:06:00.160
during back-to-back questions, especially&nbsp;
in live interviews where speed matters.&nbsp;

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:05.840
And there’s no multi-speaker labeling - Cluely&nbsp;
only recognizes either your microphone or your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:10.400
computer audio, not both at once.
Its suggested actions can also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:15.600
feel generic or off-context at times.
So if you’re looking for something more useful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:21.678
and secured, you might want to check out Fathom&nbsp;
AI notetaker, which we tested in this video here:

